# Kernel releases (uname -r) that `make install` accepts without MOOB_ALLOW_UNSUPPORTED=1.
# The rule is docs/compatibility.md section 1: a kernel is supported when the full suite and
# the KASAN job pass on it in CI, with one fstests quick run per lower filesystem (rule 3).
# The upstream 6.12.116 KASAN kernel is a test build, not an installation target, so it is not
# listed. One release per line.
